 "usage": "The template is ready to submit verbatim as `trainRecipe` on a POST to this project/version's /v2/trainings path alongside `modelType`. To tune training, set a sparse subset of the keys listed in schema.hyperparameters under template.hyperparameters \u2014 any key you omit is filled with its advice.default server-side. advice.low/high is the recommended sweep range; valid.* are hard bounds the server enforces. Add augmentation steps from schema.online_augmentation.steps to template.online_augmentation.steps; each step is submitted as {name, params: {...}} \u2014 params is required, {} when a step has no fields \u2014 with the step's listed params plus an optional params.probability between 0 and 1. To set the overall pick rate, add template.online_augmentation.probability between 0 and 1 before submitting. The template omits this optional field; when omitted, the pick rate defaults to 1. params.probability is the chance the step is applied to a picked image (default 1), so the two multiply. Submitting a trainRecipe requires the workspace's online-augmentation training entitlement or rollout access, plus an enabled deployment runtime. availability.entitled reports the access decision and availability.runtimeEnabled reports the runtime check. Access is checked again on submit; if it has changed, the request can be rejected with a 403."
